# Rendered deer-flow MCP config (contains client API key)
deploy/client-bundle/deer-flow-extensions-config.json

# Backups the installer writes when it RE-RENDERS that config.
#
# Not a tidiness rule - this one breaks the update path. install.ps1 -Update
# refuses to refresh the repo when `git status --porcelain` is non-empty, and
# --porcelain lists UNTRACKED files too. The render in step 2 writes
# deer-flow-extensions-config.json.bak.<timestamp> on the FIRST update after any
# template change, so without this line that backup makes the tree dirty, and the
# NEXT -Update silently skips the repo refresh while still pulling images. The
# machine drifts behind on all repo content with no error.
#
# The glob is specific to the config's own backups; do not widen it to
# deploy/client-bundle/*.bak.* or it would hide genuine backup files elsewhere.
deploy/client-bundle/deer-flow-extensions-config.json.bak.*
deploy/client-bundle/openviking/ov.conf.bak.*

# Deer-flow admin login credentials (per-machine, created at runtime in the
# container's local SQLite DB; NOT in .env). Never commit.
deploy/client-bundle/.deer-flow-credentials

# Cloned upstream deer-flow source used to build the frontend image
# (deploy/deer-flow-src/ → deploy/deer-flow-frontend-pacgate/Dockerfile →
# ghcr.io/jzkk720/deer-flow-frontend-pacgate:0.1.0).
# Rebuild it from the git tag; never commit the source checkout.
deploy/deer-flow-src/
# Legacy path (older build) kept ignored to avoid accidental commits.
deploy/client-bundle/deer-flow-src/

# Runtime copy of qm-pacgate staged by setup-qm.ps1 (tracked source is deploy/qm-pacgate/)
deploy/client-bundle/qm-pacgate/

# OpenViking runtime state (client-owned, per-machine)
deploy/client-bundle/openviking/ov.conf
deploy/client-bundle/openviking/workspace/

# deer-flow persistent state (live SQLite: admin password hash, threads,
# checkpoints) + pre-upgrade DB backups. NEVER commit — contains credential
# material and client chat history. This dir is the ./data/deer-flow bind mount.
deploy/client-bundle/data/

# OpenViking runtime CLI settings (per-machine, contains local state)
deploy/client-bundle/openviking/ovcli.settings.conf

# ── Credential hygiene (added 2026-09-15) ────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. A sweep on 2026-09-15 found three tracked files holding
# real, working credentials (an account password, legal portal logins, and paid
# API keys). They have been redacted, but the values remain in history and MUST
# be rotated. See plans/013-credential-rotation.md.
#
# IMPORTANT — how this block is meant to work:
#   The PRIMARY control is `scripts/detect-literal-credentials.ps1` plus the
#   pre-commit guard `scripts/assert-no-staged-secrets.ps1`, which inspect file
#   CONTENT. The filename globs below are only a secondary net.
#
#   Unanchored globs such as `*credentials*` were tried here first and caused
#   collateral damage THREE times: they swallowed
#   plans/013-credential-rotation.md and then
#   scripts/{assert-no-staged-secrets,redact-exposed-credentials,
#   detect-literal-credentials}.ps1. Keep patterns narrow, and always test a new
#   rule with `git check-ignore -v <path>` before committing it.
#
# High-signal filenames only. Note gitignore negation cannot re-include a file
# whose parent pattern already matched, so keep these patterns NARROW rather
# than relying on `!` rules.
OPERATOR*.md
*credential*.json
*credential*.yaml
*credential*.yml
*credentials.csv
*credentials.txt
*secrets.json
*secrets.yaml
*secrets.yml
*密钥表*
# Environment and key material.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.npmrc
.pypirc
.netrc
*_history
.*_history

# Generated build/delivery archives
*.zip

# Graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable)
graphify-out/


# Credential carriers (incident 2026-09-16) - never track
pacgate-ai/**/pacgate-ai-remote-handbook/OPERATOR.md
pacgate-ai/**/MCP*/
.e2e-ner-model/
